\value{
Returns an object of class \code{varmxid}, with the same general
structure as \code{\link[=FitVARMxID]{FitVARMxID()}}. The object collates the individual saved
fits and contains:
\describe{
\item{call}{Function call.}
\item{args}{List of function arguments, including \code{path}, \code{prefix},
and \code{overwrite}.}
\item{fun}{Function used (\code{"FitVARMxIDSave"}).}
\item{model}{A list of generated OpenMx models.}
\item{output}{A list of fitted OpenMx models.}
\item{converged}{A named logical vector indicating converged cases.}
\item{robust}{A list of output from \code{\link[OpenMx:imxRobustSE]{OpenMx::imxRobustSE()}}
with argument \code{details = TRUE} for each \code{id} if \code{robust = TRUE};
otherwise \code{NULL}.}
}
In addition, each individual fit is saved to disk as an \file{.Rds} file.
If a model fails for a given ID, an error object is saved as
\code{prefix_id_error.Rds}, and that ID is omitted from the returned collated
\code{varmxid} object.
}
\description{
Fits a first-order vector autoregressive model separately for each unit ID
and saves each individual fitted model object to an \file{.Rds} file.
This function fits the same individual-level models as \code{\link[=FitVARMxID]{FitVARMxID()}}, but
saves each individual fit to disk. For each unique value of \code{id}, the model
is fit using the corresponding subset of \code{data}. The fitted object for that
ID is saved to \code{path} with file name \code{prefix_id.Rds}, where \code{id} is replaced
by the unit ID value.
The value added by \code{FitVARMxIDSave()} is that the individual fits are
persisted to disk while the function still returns a collated object of
class \code{varmxid}, similar to the object returned by \code{\link[=FitVARMxID]{FitVARMxID()}}.
}
\examples{
\donttest{
# Generate data using the simStateSpace package ----------------------
set.seed(42)
n <- 5
time <- 100
p <- 2
alpha <- rep(x = 0, times = p)
beta <- 0.50 * diag(p)
psi <- 0.001 * diag(p)
psi_l <- t(chol(psi))
mu0 <- simStateSpace::SSMMeanEta(
  beta = beta,
  alpha = alpha
)
sigma0 <- simStateSpace::SSMCovEta(
  beta = beta,
  psi = psi
)
sigma0_l <- t(chol(sigma0))
sim <- simStateSpace::SimSSMVARFixed(
  n = n,
  time = time,
  mu0 = mu0,
  sigma0_l = sigma0_l,
  alpha = alpha,
  beta = beta,
  psi_l = psi_l
)
data <- as.data.frame(sim)

# Save results to a temporary directory ------------------------------
path <- tempdir()

# Fit the model with person-mean centering ---------------------------
fit <- FitVARMxIDSave(
  data = data,
  observed = paste0("y", seq_len(p)),
  id = "id",
  center = TRUE,
  path = path,
  prefix = "fitvarmx_centered"
)
print(fit)
summary(fit)
coef(fit)
vcov(fit)
converged(fit)
confint(fit)
plot(fit)
}

}
